$bog_vmap_part_map $mol_view
	- Ports are plain numbers, one each, so that a wire carrying one number
	- lands on any of them. The center is derived from `lat` and `lng`.
	zoom? 10
	lat? 59.94
	lng? 30.31
	marker? \
	zoom_min 0
	zoom_max 19
	sub /
		<= Map $mol_map_yandex
			zoom? <=> zoom_limited? 10
			center? <=> center? $mol_vector_2d<number> /
				0
				0
			objects <= objects /$mol_map_yandex_mark
	- The one mark, placed at the center and shown while `marker` has text.
	- `pos` is bound here on purpose: the class of the mark would otherwise
	- geocode its address over the network to find its position.
	Mark $mol_map_yandex_mark
		pos <= center
		title <= marker
		hint <= marker
